    oneLine: "Whether a business can meet what falls due within the year, using what it can convert to cash.",
    what: "Liquidity ratios compare short-term assets against short-term obligations. The current ratio uses all current assets. The quick ratio excludes inventory, because inventory must first be sold before it becomes cash. The cash ratio is the strictest, counting only cash and equivalents.",
